## Macros

Record a sequence of keystrokes into a register and replay it on demand.
In normal mode:

- `q{reg}`: Start recording into register `{reg}` (`a`-`z`; `A`-`Z` appends)
- `q`: Stop recording
- `@{reg}`: Play register `{reg}`
- `@@`: Replay the last played register
- `{n}@{reg}`: Play register `{reg}` `n` times
- `{n}@@`: Replay the last played register `n` times

A recorded macro is stored in a plain register, so you can bind it to a
key or wrap it in an alias with the `echo` command's `{register}`
instruction, for example `echo {register}a`. See the
[vim editor guide](https://docs.rune.build/learn/vim-editor#macros)
for recording examples.
{{- else if eq .EditorMode "helix"}}

## Macros

Record a sequence of keystrokes into a register and replay it on demand.
In normal mode:

- `Q`: Start recording into the selected register; press again to stop
- `q`: Replay the selected register
- `"{reg}Q`: Record into register `{reg}` (`a`-`z`; `A`-`Z` appends)
- `"{reg}q`: Replay register `{reg}`

A recorded macro is stored in a plain register, so you can bind it to a
key or wrap it in an alias with the `echo` command's `{register}`
instruction, for example `echo {register}a`. See the
[helix editor guide](https://docs.rune.build/learn/helix-editor#macros)
for recording examples.
{{- else if eq .EditorMode "standard"}}

## Macros

Record a sequence of keystrokes and replay it on demand:

- `<ctrl-q>`: Start recording; press again to stop (unnamed register)
- `<ctrl-shift-q>`: Play the recorded macro

The recording is stored in the unnamed register. See the
[standard editor guide](https://docs.rune.build/learn/standard-editor#macros)
for details.
{{- end}}
